---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How China AI Hub handles personal data: no accounts, no forms, no tracking, the technical logs from our hosting provider, and your rights under GDPR and CCPA."
  type="article"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: 2026-10-23</p>

    <h2>Scope of this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy explains how <strong>China AI Hub</strong> handles information in connection with
      the website at <code>sinoaihub.com</code> and its companion reference site at
      <code>data.sinoaihub.com</code> (together, "the site"). China AI Hub is an independent,
      English-language knowledge and intelligence platform about China's AI ecosystem — models,
      agents, APIs, companies, pricing, benchmarks and technology. It is a reference and research
      site, not an e-commerce store, and it does not require registration or an account.
    </p>

    <h2>Who operates the site</h2>
    <p>
      The site is operated by the China AI Hub project. The project publishes a contact point and a
      team-level byline (the <a href="/authors/">SinoAI Hub Research Team</a>); it does not publish
      a corporate legal name, registration number, or registered office. Contact for privacy
      matters is the same as the general contact point:
      Martin.W — <a href="mailto:admin@sinoaihub.com">admin@sinoaihub.com</a>. The project has
      <strong>no appointed Data Protection Officer</strong>; where a supervisory authority or a data
      subject needs a specific contact, use the email above.
    </p>

    <h2>Our approach in one sentence</h2>
    <p>
      We practice data minimization by design: the site collects no personal data through forms,
      accounts or tracking, so there is very little personal data to protect in the first place.
      The sections below explain the few narrow situations in which information reaches us.
    </p>

    <h2>Personal data we collect</h2>
    <p>
      The site is designed to collect as little information as possible. It has
      <strong>no user accounts, no login, and no contact forms</strong>. There is no newsletter, no
      comment system, and no user-generated content. Concretely, the only situations in which
      information reaches us are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email you send us.</strong> If you email <code>admin@sinoaihub.com</code> (for
        example, to report a correction), we receive the contents of your message and your email
        address. We use this only to read and respond to your message. We do not add it to a
        mailing list, and we do not sell or share it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>WhatsApp messages you initiate.</strong> The footer contains a WhatsApp link
        (<code>wa.me/8613323237275</code>). If you click it, the conversation takes place on
        WhatsApp's platform and is governed by <em>WhatsApp's</em> privacy policy, not this one.
        We receive only the messages you choose to send through WhatsApp.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Standard technical logs from our hosting provider.</strong> The site is served by
        Cloudflare Pages. Like most hosts, Cloudflare may record standard technical data (IP
        address, user-agent string, request path and time) for security, abuse prevention and
        availability. See "Hosting and server logs" below.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> otherwise collect names, contact details, location data, device
      identifiers, or behavioral profiles, because the site has no mechanism to do so.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No accounts or profiles</strong> — there is no login, registration, or user profile.</li>
      <li><strong>No analytics or advertising tracking</strong> — we run no Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, Hotjar, Clarity, Plausible, Fathom, Matomo, PostHog, or any equivalent.</li>
      <li><strong>No first-party tracking cookies</strong> — see the <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>No contact form data</strong> — the site has no forms to submit.</li>
      <li><strong>No payment or billing data</strong> — the site sells nothing and processes no payments.</li>
      <li><strong>No location or device data</strong> — beyond the standard technical logs noted above, we do not collect geolocation, device fingerprints, or advertising identifiers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      China AI Hub does not set tracking, analytics or advertising cookies. Our hosting provider
      (Cloudflare) may set strictly necessary technical measures at the infrastructure level, such
      as a bot-management security token (<code>__cf_bm</code>) or its email-protection feature,
      which decodes our obfuscated contact email address in your browser. These measures keep the
      site operational and secure and are not used to profile visitors, serve ads, or build
      marketing audiences. A full classification is in the <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>
      The only information we use is (a) the contents of email or WhatsApp messages you send, which
      we use to respond to you and to correct or improve the site where you report an error, and
      (b) the technical logs described above, which are used by our host for security, abuse
      prevention and availability. We do not use any of this information for marketing, profiling,
      advertising, or automated decision-making. We do not combine correspondence with technical
      logs to build a picture of an individual, and we do not build or maintain visitor profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>. Cloudflare may keep standard
      technical logs (IP address, user agent, request time, and the resource requested) for
      security and abuse prevention. We do not access or combine these logs to identify or profile
      individuals, and we do not use them for any commercial purpose. Cloudflare's own processing
      of this data is governed by Cloudflare's privacy policy; for questions about their
      infrastructure-level processing, contact Cloudflare directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Because we do not collect personal data through the site, there is effectively no
      site-collected personal data for us to retain. Email correspondence is kept only as long as
      needed to handle the matter and is not archived into a marketing system. Technical logs held
      by Cloudflare are retained by Cloudflare according to its own retention schedules and are
      outside our control. If you contact us and would like your correspondence deleted, tell us
      and we will remove what we hold.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties and onward transfers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — provides hosting and security. It may process technical logs
        described above as our data processor.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>WhatsApp (Meta)</strong> — if you contact us via WhatsApp, Meta processes your
        messages under Meta's own terms. Clicking the WhatsApp button is entirely your choice.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vendor and source websites</strong> — throughout the site we link to official
        vendor documentation, model cards, pricing pages and other third-party sources. When you
        follow those links, the destination site's own privacy practices apply.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data, and we do not disclose it to advertisers, data brokers, or any
      third party for their own marketing use. The third parties above are infrastructure or
      communication channels, not data buyers.
    </p>

    <h2>Cross-border transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served through Cloudflare's globally distributed network, which means your
      requests may be handled by servers outside your country, and Cloudflare may store technical
      logs in jurisdictions other than your own. This is the only cross-border element. We collect
      no personal data ourselves, so there is no separately stored personal data for us to transfer.
      If you email us, your message is handled by our email provider; see the mail provider's
      policy for its location and retention.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal bases under GDPR (EEA and UK)</h2>
    <p>
      For visitors in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom, we process any personal
      data on the following bases:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — operating a secure, available website (technical
        logs via our host) and responding to correspondence you initiate. We have balanced these
        interests against your rights and concluded they are proportionate given that we collect
        no tracking data and no site-generated personal data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your request to contact us</strong> — when you email or message us, we process
        that message to respond, on the basis of taking steps at your request.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not rely on consent for analytics or marketing because we run none. We do not process
      special-category data, and we do not make decisions based on automated processing.
    </p>

    <h2>CCPA / CPRA (California)</h2>
    <p>
      For California residents, China AI Hub does not "sell" or "share" personal information in the
      sense of the California Consumer Privacy Act, and it does not use or disclose sensitive
      personal information for the purpose of inferring characteristics. The site collects no
      personal information through forms or tracking. If you nevertheless believe we hold personal
      information about you (for example, from an email you sent), you may request access,
      correction, or deletion by emailing <a href="mailto:admin@sinoaihub.com">admin@sinoaihub.com</a>.
      We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Other jurisdictions</h2>
    <p>
      This policy describes the project's practices generally, but different jurisdictions grant
      different rights (for example, under PIPL in mainland China, the UK GDPR, or the privacy laws
      of Australia, Canada and Brazil). Because the site collects no personal data itself, in most
      cases the practical answer is the same: there is nothing for us to access, correct or delete
      beyond any correspondence you have sent us. If you believe a specific right applies to you,
      contact us and we will respond in accordance with the law that governs your situation.
    </p>

    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
      Some browsers send a "Do Not Track" (DNT) signal. Because we run no tracking or analytics at
      all, there is nothing for a DNT signal to disable; the site's behavior is the same whether or
      not DNT is set. See the <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> for details on the strictly
      necessary technical measures set by our host.
    </p>

    <h2>Automated decision-making</h2>
    <p>
      We do not use personal data to make any decision that produces legal or similarly significant
      effects concerning you, and we do not profile visitors. The site's only automation operates
      on <em>public vendor data</em> (re-fetching sources to verify model specifications and
      prices), not on personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a technical reference for professionals, researchers and developers. It is not
      directed at children under 13 (or the applicable minimum age in your jurisdiction), and we do
      not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has provided us
      personal data, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static content with no login or database of user data, which materially reduces
      the personal-data surface. Delivery and transport are handled by Cloudflare over HTTPS. No
      security measure can guarantee absolute security; because we hold no site-collected personal
      data, the practical risk to visitors is correspondingly low. If we become aware of a security
      incident affecting personal data we do hold (for example, correspondence), we will address it
      and notify affected individuals where required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>AI-generated images</h2>
    <p>
      Illustrations on entity pages are AI-generated (labeled in image credits, e.g. "Seedream")
      and contain no personal data. The site's text is researched and written by the SinoAI Hub
      Research Team; analysis is labeled, and automated tooling is used only in the verification
      workflow described in the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>. See the
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> for how AI use is disclosed.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or
      object to the processing of your personal data, and (in the EEA/UK) to data portability and
      to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. Because the site collects no personal data
      itself, in most cases there is nothing to exercise these rights over. To the extent you have
      contacted us and want access to, correction of, or deletion of that correspondence, email us
      and we will respond within a reasonable time. To help us locate anything we might hold, tell
      us the email address you used and, if relevant, the approximate date of your message.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the site's practices or applicable law change. The "Last
      updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Material changes
      will be reflected here; we do not maintain a mailing list to push notifications, so please
      review this page when you have concerns.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or how your information is handled: Martin.W —
      <a href="mailto:admin@sinoaihub.com">admin@sinoaihub.com</a>. Related pages:
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> · <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> ·
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/about/">About</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
